          <li><strong>30% Chance:</strong> Inherits Parent B's exact IV value.</li>
          <li><strong>40% Chance:</strong> Rolls a random value between 0 and 100.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          When both parents possess 100 IV in a stat, the combined chance of the offspring inheriting a 100 IV is <strong>60.4%</strong> (30% + 30% + [40% × 1/101]). To achieve a perfect triple-max (100/100/100) Pal, you have roughly a <strong>22% hatch probability</strong> (~1 in 4.5 eggs) when breeding two perfect parents.
        </p>
